The agent completed and committed the boss-duel design proposal as `3836b95` on `feature/boss-duel`. It also added an index entry to `docs/README.md`. Nothing was merged or pushed, and no gameplay code was changed.

The proposal identifies two bugs in the current Feint move: its real swing has only a 0.4-second warning, below the 0.45-second minimum, and it does not mark its warning, so `TelegraphFrac` remains `-1` and skews the boss's `EarlyRatio` statistic.

The design recommends a decision-focused boss fight with visible Focus and Poise systems, a universal commit point with at least 450 ms of reaction time, adaptive but bounded boss behavior, an attackable companion with targeting safeguards, and rule-based mid-fight behavior. The LLM should only configure bounded personality parameters and generate taunts between fights.

The document includes research references, a four-milestone implementation plan, and several open questions, including the reaction-time floor, whether the companion can be downed, whether to include the second character pairing, whether to show Focus, branch ownership for `Poise`, `Threat`, and `DamageTaken`, and potential key conflicts.

